% composition-series: Ontario Listening Bridges — set 1
% composition-grade: 2
% composition-elements: pitch (do-re-mi-so-la pentatonic and high do), duration (half and whole notes), texture (melody over do-so bordun), form (AB)
% composition-listen: Stella Chiweshe — "Chachimurenga"
% composition-listen-url: https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Stella+Chiweshe+Chachimurenga
% composition-bridge: Follow one repeating interlocking figure while the voice moves independently; notice cyclical rather than chord-by-chord listening.
% composition-context: Stella Chiweshe is a major Zimbabwean mbira performer. The recording can introduce mbira dzavadzimu, interlocking parts and cultural responsibility; this original pentatonic school piece is not mbira repertoire.
% composition-distance: Original melody and bordun; no kushaura/kutsinhira part, lyric or recording phrase is transcribed.
% improv: {"id":"A","bars":"1-2","role":"melody player over bordun","prompt":"Mirror or cross the contour?","choices":["mirror it","reverse it","hold high do"],"replyBars":2}
% improv: {"id":"B","bars":"5-6","role":"ostinato group","prompt":"How does the cycle change?","choices":["same","one rest","swap do and so"],"replyBars":2}
% dossier-honesty: Original pentatonic bordun study; mbira is the listening subject, not the claimed style of the draft.
% dossier-licence: Draft original; reference recording remains copyrighted.
% dossier-respect: Do not detach mbira dzavadzimu from Shona history and living practice or market a xylophone ostinato as "African mbira music."
% dossier-review: Zimbabwean mbira educator and Grade 2 teacher.
